  "functions": [
    "FUNC.DAYS360"
  ],
  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "DAYS360 treats serial 60 as 1900-02-29 and differs by 1 day on leap-Feb-29 to non-leap-Feb-28",
  "statement": "In the 1900 date system, DAYS360(start_date, end_date, [method]) maps serial 60 to the fictitious 1900-02-29 and truncates fractional serials. On 2024-02-29 (serial 45351) to 2025-02-28 (serial 45716), Excel 16.0.20527.20088 returns 358 under the US/NASD method (FALSE/omitted) and 359 under the European method (TRUE), because US/NASD adjusts start day 29 to 30 while leaving non-leap end day 28 unadjusted when both dates are end-of-February. All 4,564 full-bank DAYS360 rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in Excel 16.0.20527.20088 (f2_rows rows 131-132) and Excel 16.0 build 20430 (CalcFunc-Evidence cache/oracle-20430/build-20430/DAYS360.jsonl.gz); 4,564/4,564 full-bank rows match.",
